WEBVTT

00:02:29.522 --> 00:02:31.558
And I want you to stop saying that."

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.099
About 20 years ago,

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:40.174
I was asked by my editors
at the "New York Times Magazine"

00:02:40.198 --> 00:02:42.894
to write a piece about Deaf culture.

00:02:42.918 --> 00:02:44.324
And I was rather taken aback.

00:02:44.348 --> 00:02:46.652
I had thought of deafness
entirely as an illness:

00:02:46.676 --> 00:02:48.636
those poor people, they couldn't hear,

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.280
they lacked hearing,
and what could we do for them?

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.798
And then I went out into the Deaf world.

00:02:53.822 --> 00:02:55.703
I went to Deaf clubs.

00:02:55.727 --> 00:03:00.105
I saw performances of Deaf theater
and of Deaf poetry.